        </div>

        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Running cost is not a real consideration —
            one to six dollars a month covers almost every household.</strong>
            Calculate from actual draw rather than the rating plate, and remember
            that your own electricity rate matters more than which machine you
            bought.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            The electrical detail worth acting on is the circuit: a grounded
            outlet, no extension lead, and surge protection for the controller
            board. Keep the deck lubricated using the
            <a href="/treadmill-belt-lubrication/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">lubrication guide</a>,
            and if the machine is already dead, start with
            <a href="/treadmill-wont-turn-on/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">will not turn on</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
